WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
A man lights a cigarette at a bus stop.

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.750
The smoke drifts over three
strangers waiting beside him.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.130
Worldwide, tobacco kills
over 7 million people a year.

4
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.190
Over 1.6 million of them are non-smokers,

5
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.430
exposed to second-hand smoke.

6
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.090
They never bought a thing.

7
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.720
So when a product harms people
nearby who never bought it,

8
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.110
why does the market sell too much?

9
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.060
In this mission, you'll separate
the benefit to the buyer

10
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.980
from the benefit to society,

11
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.050
and draw both as curves.

12
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.620
Then you'll turn up the
harm in a graph lab,

13
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.030
and test your prediction of what moves.

14
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.480
Your mission: find out why
the market sells too much,

15
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.800
and how big the loss to society is.
